# Palabra production release

When the user asks to release, ship, or deploy to production, follow this exact flow.

## 1. GitHub release trigger

```bash
git commit
git tag
git push
```

Push both the branch and the version tag (e.g. `v1.1.9`). That goes to GitHub and starts the worker that builds the Docker image.

## 2. Wait for Docker build

Wait until the GitHub Actions / Docker build for that version finishes successfully before deploying.

## 3. Deploy on gate

```bash
ssh gate
cd /root/stacks/palabra
docker compose pull
docker compose down
docker compose up -d
```

That is the full production rollout. Do not invent alternate deploy paths unless the user asks.
